{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses","id":1562476,"title":"[6E] Senses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-02T06:45:35-07:00","id":1562476,"title":"[6E] Senses","content":"Anybody remember when back when, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1284912-v5-why-not-better-dark-vision\">I brought up sharper senses for vampires</a>?<br /> <br /> So, according to the new 6E Player Packet:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Senses. Your senses are no sharper or different than they were when you were a mortal.<br /> You can, however, heighten your awareness through Discipline powers (see Step 6) or by surging your blood to enhance your natural Attributes (see step 5) </div> </div> </div>This is a &quot;fuck you&quot; to the players, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T06:51:24-07:00","id":1562478,"title":"","content":"Wut? I don't follow the reasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T07:16:45-07:00","id":1562483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses#post1562476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a &quot;fuck you&quot; to the players, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be if it was a consensus, but I thought you had noticed by your thread this is not.<br /> <br /> The rules already accept as fair interpretation that normal human eye adjustment to the dark works, so one possible problem is people who take certain situations as darker in rule terms than intended.<br /> <br /> Case in point, complete darkness in the game is deep caves, which is something you simply can't get in a city and even most rural areas. How many times in your life have you been in a place so dark that even after an entire hour of adaptation you literally couldn't see anything?<br /> <br /> But that aside, while I do agree that I'd prefer this, it was deliberately not part of VtM and a lot of players prefer it this way, most others not even thinking about it. So... No, this isn't a fuck you to no one.<br /> <br /> You can play Requiem if you want more proper night hunter themes, as I do, or just liberally take its rules for VtM, as many others do. VtR follows a conceptualization of vampires more in line with this, including rules to track blood and noticing heartbeats.<br /> <br /> VtM isn't like that and we do not represent the actual majority opinion among players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T08:36:04-07:00","id":1562490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562483#post1562483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would be if it was a consensus, but I thought you had noticed by your thread this is not.<br /> <br /> The rules already accept as fair interpretation that normal human eye adjustment to the dark works, so one possible problem is people who take certain situations as darker in rule terms than intended.<br /> <br /> Case in point, complete darkness in the game is deep caves, which is something you simply can't get in a city and even most rural areas. How many times in your life have you been in a place so dark that even after an entire hour of adaptation you literally couldn't see anything?<br /> <br /> But that aside, while I do agree that I'd prefer this, it was deliberately not part of VtM and a lot of players prefer it this way, most others not even thinking about it. So... No, this isn't a fuck you to no one.<br /> <br /> You can play Requiem if you want more proper night hunter themes, as I do, or just liberally take its rules for VtM, as many others do. VtR follows a conceptualization of vampires more in line with this, including rules to track blood and noticing heartbeats.<br /> <br /> VtM isn't like that and we do not represent the actual majority opinion among players.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I mean, I have nothing again houseruling or assuming that vampires should have darkvision but it's not something that was ever true in VtM. Otherwise Eyes of the Beast would make no sense as Discipline power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T09:45:20-07:00","id":1562492,"title":"","content":"Don't subscribe motives to people that we haven't met Serpent Axis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T15:23:52-07:00","id":1562509,"title":"","content":"So, after almost 10 years, I have to rephrase and reiterate this again, it seems.<br /> <br /> I'll try to bring you along for a journey to my reasoning:<ul><li>Vampire is a horror game of a different kind of horror - the protagonists, the player characters, are the monsters and the game (supposedly) focuses on their personal, internal struggles as opposed to adventure-style obstacles and external challenges that require or inflict no moral or dramatic effect on the character.</li> <li>Vampires are creatures of the night and darkness, and several kinds of vampires (Nosferatu, etc.) are supposed to be inured to dark, poorly lit locations - like movie-style sewer systems. They are nocturnal predators.</li> <li>The mechanics of the game should serve its themes and accentuate the increasing alienation of the characters from the mortals around them, and that includes sensory aberrations (<i>&quot;only when your friend asks you why you've been sitting in the dark that you realize the light was off&quot;</i>, or, <i>&quot;the copperish scent is overwhelming, sweet and inviting. When you open the door, your companion turns and nearly keels over. To you, the smells coming off the fly-covered, shriveled man on the kitchen floor are a mix between aged liquor and the intoxicating aroma of fear and despair, but the scents have lost some of their luster - like a meal going bad&quot;</i>).</li> <li>Light and Darkness are thematic and symbolic. The Light is the realm of vitality and life, hope, truth, it is the tool of heroes and mortals huddling together against the night. The Dark is the realm of predators and danger, death, decay, secrets, treachery and unnatural things with too many teeth. Vampires are Of the Dark. They are the predator lurking in the shadows, watching the mortals huddled around the campfire. This is a personal idea of mine, to have this theme of light vs dark, and it doesn't necessarily exclude vampires from ever using lights (it can be symbolic, holding onto hope) but I don't think that they should be using or relying on it like the thematic mortal heroes.</li> <li>Heightened Senses and Eyes of the Beast are not precious, perfect powers whose loss would be terrible for the game, as you can simply replace them with more useful effects. But even if you wanted to keep them, you could because:</li> <li>I didn't say &quot;give them Darkvision&quot;, I said &quot;Low-Light Vision would be fine&quot;. Both Heightened Senses and Eyes of the Beast give you the equivalent of Darkvision or better abilities, plus other benefits such as premonition or bonuses to intimidation.</li> </ul>So... Yeah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T15:59:44-07:00","id":1562513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562509#post1562509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after almost 10 years, I have to rephrase and reiterate this again, it seems.<br /> <br /> I'll try to bring you along for a journey to my reasoning:<ul><li>Vampire is a horror game of a different kind of horror - the protagonists, the player characters, are the monsters and the game (supposedly) focuses on their personal, internal struggles as opposed to adventure-style obstacles and external challenges that require or inflict no moral or dramatic effect on the character.</li> <li>Vampires are creatures of the night and darkness, and several kinds of vampires (Nosferatu, etc.) are supposed to be inured to dark, poorly lit locations - like movie-style sewer systems. They are nocturnal predators.</li> <li>The mechanics of the game should serve its themes and accentuate the increasing alienation of the characters from the mortals around them, and that includes sensory aberrations (<i>&quot;only when your friend asks you why you've been sitting in the dark that you realize the light was off&quot;</i>, or, <i>&quot;the copperish scent is overwhelming, sweet and inviting. When you open the door, your companion turns and nearly keels over. To you, the smells coming off the fly-covered, shriveled man on the kitchen floor are a mix between aged liquor and the intoxicating aroma of fear and despair, but the scents have lost some of their luster - like a meal going bad&quot;</i>).</li> <li>Light and Darkness are thematic and symbolic. The Light is the realm of vitality and life, hope, truth, it is the tool of heroes and mortals huddling together against the night. The Dark is the realm of predators and danger, death, decay, secrets, treachery and unnatural things with too many teeth. Vampires are Of the Dark. They are the predator lurking in the shadows, watching the mortals huddled around the campfire. This is a personal idea of mine, to have this theme of light vs dark, and it doesn't necessarily exclude vampires from ever using lights (it can be symbolic, holding onto hope) but I don't think that they should be using or relying on it like the thematic mortal heroes.</li> <li>Heightened Senses and Eyes of the Beast are not precious, perfect powers whose loss would be terrible for the game, as you can simply replace them with more useful effects. But even if you wanted to keep them, you could because:</li> <li>I didn't say &quot;give them Darkvision&quot;, I said &quot;Low-Light Vision would be fine&quot;. Both Heightened Senses and Eyes of the Beast give you the equivalent of Darkvision or better abilities, plus other benefits such as premonition or bonuses to intimidation.</li> </ul>So... Yeah</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because they <i>should</i> get dark vision, doesn't mean that they do. If they've never had dark vision, then how can it be an &quot;F you&quot; to the players that Cainites still don't get it now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T16:13:46-07:00","id":1562514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562513#post1562513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just because they <i>should</i> get dark vision, doesn't mean that they do. If they've never had dark vision, then how can it be an &quot;F you&quot; to the players that Cainites still don't get it now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there sure are a lot of &quot;they <i>should </i>but they <i>don't</i>&quot;s in VtM. <br /> <br /> And as for the how it's an FU to us, that's because this is happening after Requiem's changes and while I'm not haughty enough to think any of the devs have ever read our posts in that thread, surely if you make a new edition of Vampire and you have all the work that's already been done to build upon, you should be improving and seeking to innovate.<br /> Instead, this feels like a step back. And they purposely went through the trouble of mentioning the senses thing right in the front. <br /> So to me it kind of felt like &quot;oh, you wanted the innovation from Requem? well, how about no, instead?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T16:27:03-07:00","id":1562517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562509#post1562509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after almost 10 years, I have to rephrase and reiterate this again, it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you don't. Your reasoning is perfectly clear and there are people who agree with it. I do, by the way.<br /> <br /> But there are a lot of people who don't. That's the end of it.<br /> <br /> If you can't understand the concept of your reasoning not being universal among players by the fact you got people telling you they disagree with it, then it can't be helped, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T16:27:45-07:00","id":1562518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562514#post1562514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, there sure are a lot of &quot;they <i>should </i>but they <i>don't</i>&quot;s in VtM.<br /> <br /> And as for the how it's an FU to us, that's because this is happening after Requiem's changes and while I'm not haughty enough to think any of the devs have ever read our posts in that thread, surely if you make a new edition of Vampire and you have all the work that's already been done to build upon, you should be improving and seeking to innovate.<br /> Instead, this feels like a step back. And they purposely went through the trouble of mentioning the senses thing right in the front.<br /> So to me it kind of felt like &quot;oh, you wanted the innovation from Requem? well, how about no, instead?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Look, maybe there is some arguments to justify the change you want but those are not it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Instead, it feels like a step back.&quot; Again, what? They did not change anything so it cannot be a step back as they are in the same spot as they were in V5 and all the previous editions. Eyes of the Beast were in every edition since the first and they are kinda staple power.<br /> <br /> I don't like going for anecdotal evidence but you are getting enraged on behalf of the players yet almost everyone in this thread is disagreeing with you.<br /> <br /> The guy who wanted to make new Requiem is no longer line developer for Vampire and the new guy is known for OSR so if you were expecting that V6 will be more VtR than V5 I have bad news for you.<br /> <br /> But ultimately there are plenty criticism to throw at V6 playtest and &quot;vampires still can't see in the dark&quot; is one of them. I just can't understand the level of vitriol for such trivial thing. I would maybe have more understanding if it was something that they walked back on but no, it's just a holdover from previous editions. I am just baffled how emotional your reaction is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T21:36:40-07:00","id":1562528,"title":"","content":"The problem is that this is not a requiem/not requiem issue.<br /> <br /> Vtm need vampires to see better than mortals in the dark for the setting to make sense.<br /> <br /> Vampires existed aeons before gaslighting or electric lights. They were always purely nocturnal and the only way for a human eye to do all the reading and writing they do in the night (not mentioning entering a house to feed on sleeping people without walking on every abandonned tools) isto use torches and candles. So the very things that can easily kill a kindred and for which they have an instinctual fear.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the nosferatu are supposed to live in caverns, underground and deep sewers... Without auspex or eyes of the beast.<br /> <br /> So I get Serpent Axis' reaction.<br /> <br /> Forgetting that detail in earlier \u00e9ditions is an acceptable mishap. Forgetting that detail in dark ages was... More touchy. Refusing to mention it in v20 or V5 is essentially putting that detail to GMs, so that's fine, but definitively telling bow that kindred don't see better?<br /> <br /> Yes folks, every assamite assassin was utterly d\u00e9pendant on a city guard being nice enough to leave torches to not trip on every single things in a medieval street. And every kindred feeding on sleeping parents without protean, auspex or abyss mysticisme has to make soak rolls for the ammount of lego they step on and the ammount of fourniture their toes impact.<br /> <br /> Seriously, they couldn't just either state a system less &quot;vampires see better in the dark&quot; or just... Follow the gameline tradition of never mentionning that detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T00:41:32-07:00","id":1562536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562528#post1562528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vtm need vampires to see better than mortals in the dark for the setting to make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. And isn't the point, either.<br /> <br /> As much as I think vampires should have it, it's neither necessary for the fans nor necessary for credibility.<br /> <br /> People in the Middle Ages could walk in the dark of the night just fine. They did it, regularly, not only with torches.<br /> <br /> Human eyes can get used to the dark just fine. Without much light pollution the moon and stars illuminate surprisingly well. And there was nothing like legos in the floor, first because toys weren't like that, second because they wouldn't be around in the floor, given that they would also walk around in the dark some hours in the night.<br /> <br /> People didn't really walked around with torches all the time at night, that would depend on where they would wander. And vampires can use candles to read and write like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Cave dwellers can also find all sorts of manners to walk around, including use other senses. It's something people do even today.<br /> <br /> But the most important part:<br /> <br /> <u><b>IT'S YOUR OPINION, NOT A FUCKING UNANIMITY</b></u><br /> <br /> You're demanding something as if your wishes were objectively and obviously superior for any player, and ignoring the other actual players that don't think the same.<br /> <br /> This kind of reasoning is what gave us V5 in the first place as a divisive thing that pissed a lot more fans than those items catered to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T02:41:27-07:00","id":1562542,"title":"","content":"Ok. I'll accept that universally, and barring Disciplines or Merits that change it, vampires have the same senses as mortals in VtM. <br /> <br /> I didn't mean to offend anyone by this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T03:39:07-07:00","id":1562546,"title":"","content":"I perfer that Kindred have three in clan disciplines to start with and that they have to learn others over time to make things more dramatic and interesting. How far do you want to enhance your senses before the drawbacks outweigh any benefits as the modern world would harder to deal with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T07:34:40-07:00","id":1562553,"title":"","content":"I personally like Kindred Senses from VTR2e, and use them in my VTM games. I would also make them a thing in V6, but it's not up to me. However, they have made things easier by saying vamps no longer freak out when they see lit cigarettes or candles. So this actually makes the Dark Ages more plausible as a result. The fact they're planning ahead for Dark Ages may mean they've already considered this fact in that context, in fact.<br /> <br /> As for additional Disciplines, I wonder whether you might also get a discount for one other Discipline based on your sire (since you'd learn it from their vitae)? This would allow those clans with out of clan blood magic to finally learn it in-clan.<br /> <br /> It's not necessary, by any means, but it adds a bit of customisation to clans and means those without unique Disciplines don't feel too left behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T08:09:32-07:00","id":1562558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562536#post1562536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it doesn't. And isn't the point, either.<br /> <br /> As much as I think vampires should have it, it's neither necessary for the fans nor necessary for credibility.<br /> <br /> People in the Middle Ages could walk in the dark of the night just fine. They did it, regularly, not only with torches.<br /> <br /> Human eyes can get used to the dark just fine. Without much light pollution the moon and stars illuminate surprisingly well. And there was nothing like legos in the floor, first because toys weren't like that, second because they wouldn't be around in the floor, given that they would also walk around in the dark some hours in the night.<br /> <br /> People didn't really walked around with torches all the time at night, that would depend on where they would wander. And vampires can use candles to read and write like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Cave dwellers can also find all sorts of manners to walk around, including use other senses. It's something people do even today.<br /> <br /> But the most important part:<br /> <br /> <u><b>IT'S YOUR OPINION, NOT A FUCKING UNANIMITY</b></u><br /> <br /> You're demanding something as if your wishes were objectively and obviously superior for any player, and ignoring the other actual players that don't think the same.<br /> <br /> This kind of reasoning is what gave us V5 in the first place as a divisive thing that pissed a lot more fans than those items catered to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You might want to ton\u00e9 down things a little. Since V6 announcement you're all over the place with a pretty agressive mindset.<br /> <br /> No, it's not just an opinion. VTM was clearly written with the assumption, since it was a modern day setting, that there's lights everywhere.<br /> <br /> The human eye is not that adaptative. Simple exemple, my village, in order to make \u00e9conomies, cuts external lights past 11 pm.<br /> <br /> And as soon as you have a shared of clouds to hide the moon, you see *nothing*.not a step in front of you outside.<br /> <br /> Same every time blackouts happens.<br /> <br /> Even when the full moon shine in a clear nightsky, you cannot see anything as soon as there's shadow, if anything. It sabotage one's vision in the dark as the eye has to try to adapt again to obscurity.<br /> <br /> No, kindred can't just use candles when you have rules on how they easily freaks out when close to one and when *even touching one by accident* can cause them to combust.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T13:01:36-07:00","id":1562573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562558#post1562558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You might want to ton\u00e9 down things a little. Since V6 announcement you're all over the place with a pretty agressive mindset.<br /> <br /> No, it's not just an opinion. VTM was clearly written with the assumption, since it was a modern day setting, that there's lights everywhere.<br /> <br /> The human eye is not that adaptative. Simple exemple, my village, in order to make \u00e9conomies, cuts external lights past 11 pm.<br /> <br /> And as soon as you have a shared of clouds to hide the moon, you see *nothing*.not a step in front of you outside.<br /> <br /> Same every time blackouts happens.<br /> <br /> Even when the full moon shine in a clear nightsky, you cannot see anything as soon as there's shadow, if anything. It sabotage one's vision in the dark as the eye has to try to adapt again to obscurity.<br /> <br /> No, kindred can't just use candles when you have rules on how they easily freaks out when close to one and when *even touching one by accident* can cause them to combust.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, there were two editions of Dark Ages setting and there was no dark vision there either. And Eyes of the Beast was always a power that has existed. <br /> <br /> Second thing, there is this thing called evolution. You can be sure that human sight was sharper like a thousand years ago because seeing in relative dark was more vital for survival. Also, even without electric lights night is not pitch black, you have light reflecting off the moon, stars. <br /> <br /> Thirdly, V6 is already saying that small fire is not going to cause Rotschreck so there.<br /> <br /> But most important, it's not a big deal, you can easily houserule that vampires can see in the dark. As I said, I understand that it might be an issue for some people but it's an issue with a simple solution demanding no effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T15:10:23-07:00","id":1562583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562553#post1562553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally like Kindred Senses from VTR2e, and use them in my VTM games.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> However, they have made things easier by saying vamps no longer freak out when they see lit cigarettes or candles. So this actually makes the Dark Ages more plausible as a result.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> As for additional Disciplines, I wonder whether you might also get a discount for one other Discipline based on your sire (since you'd learn it from their vitae)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I use VtR2nd Kindred senses, too. No need to force the corebook to change a setting assumption.<br /> <br /> With you needing a bonfire up close to start rolling for R\u00f6tschreck, not only candles but most utility fires are open for vampires. A torch or even a fireplace are perfectly within reach.<br /> <br /> For additional Disciplines, they're doing that with Sire Type. Each gives you some a list of Disciplines to choose a 4th dot that's unrelated to your in-clans. Usually a list of 3, but Adoptive Sire and Broodmate let you chose any clan and take one of their in-clans, so you're only without access to something they make to be OoC for everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562558#post1562558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to ton\u00e9 down things a little. Since V6 announcement you're all over the place with a pretty agressive mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you also speak a language that uses \u00e9 and similar, nice!<br /> <br /> You're right about me being aggressive lately and I am sorry for that elsewhere. It's unrelated to V6 itself and actually has to do with work, just fyi, but bad nonetheless.<br /> <br /> I won't tone down here, though, because I find this extremely disrespectful, as I'll explain below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562558#post1562558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not just an opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition it is, because the question isn't if humans can reliably see in the dark of the night or not.<br /> <br /> The question is if the player community sees a problem in it and if it fits the artistic choices of the setting.<br /> <br /> It's a fictional setting. If vision at night is handwaved, that's that. You may not like it, but it is an opinion because there's no objective definition of what the fictional setting has to do about it.<br /> <br /> And it so happens that no matter how good your vision is, it's not shared by a significant number of players or by the authors. The game has an assumption, the authors are committed to this assumption and most players are on board with it and happy with a well established rule that you need Protean 1 to see in the dark.<br /> <br /> When you <i><b>demand</b></i> a change in the core book and treats this as an obligation, you're saying the interests of all those people don't matter, it has to conform to your specifications. <i><b>That</b></i> is what I'm against.<br /> <br /> V5 was built upon this principle: my version of the game is the one that counts, no one else's.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562558#post1562558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The human eye is not that adaptative. Simple exemple, my village, in order to make \u00e9conomies, cuts external lights past 11 pm.<br /> <br /> And as soon as you have a shared of clouds to hide the moon, you see *nothing*.not a step in front of you outside.<br /> <br /> Same every time blackouts happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a simple example because it's a very specific example, and all the problems arise from this specificity.<br /> <br /> How frequently is the night sky overcast in any inhabited place on Earth, or even in Europe? How was it for someone whose eyes didn't had to adapt to excess light to begin with? How was it for people that had to go through this all their lives every night?<br /> <br /> Medieval people didn't burn candles and torches the whole time every night. They dealt with everything you see in your village without light.<br /> <br /> Sure, they wouldn't venture outside without a torch in darker nights, but that had more with seeing at some distance than walking itself. But inside the house people would walk around without lights from time to time and that weren't a problem. Modern people can still do that with enough preparation to get used to it, which isn't what's happening in your village.<br /> <br /> We have blackouts around here too, by the way. Not to common nowadays, but you're not the only one with experience walking the streets or inside home at night without any light. I can manage it fine, though find it a little unnerving.<br /> <br /> You're being forced by circumstances to experience some of this adaptation every night, which sucks, but you're not experiencing every form it takes in every circumstance. And a vampire in the medieval wouldn't just see as well as everyone else, they'd be used to the same conditions and limitations. And possibly avoid invading homes when the sky is overcast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562558#post1562558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, kindred can't just use candles when you have rules on how they easily freaks out when close to one and when *even touching one by accident* can cause them to combust.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... Except that they <i><b>did</b></i> correct that.<br /> <br /> First that it wasn't as terrible in the old rules. It was up to the ST when to call for it and the Diff was quite low for small flames, so vampires did use fire. And we see this repeatedly in the fiction.<br /> <br /> Second that touching fire couldn't cause them to combust, never did. I don't know where you are taking this from, but fire in the rules just causes to vampires the exact same damage or causes to mortals. No rules for being set aflame.<br /> <br /> But more importantly: V6 Playtest did stipulate that you need close proximity (\u22642 meters) to a bonfire to start rolling for R\u00f6tschreck. So now medieval light sources are all within reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T06:25:24-07:00","id":1562632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562583#post1562583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For additional Disciplines, they're doing that with Sire Type. Each gives you some a list of Disciplines to choose a 4th dot that's unrelated to your in-clans. Usually a list of 3, but Adoptive Sire and Broodmate let you chose any clan and take one of their in-clans, so you're only without access to something they make to be OoC for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more that you might extend the discount on a permanent basis. I.e., everyone gets their three clan Disciplines at the reduced price, as well as one other inherited from their sire at the same price. Those four Disciplines would then always cost current rating x 5 instead of x7.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of instances where a bloodline commonly gets something out-of-clan (usually blood magic) where a fourth &quot;in-clan&quot; Discipline (at least in terms of price) would be beneficial. Then you can have Revised-era Ahrimanes with the core Disciplines of Animalism, Auspex and Protean, with Thaumaturgy as their &quot;sire&quot; Discipline, and it's a bit more manageable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T06:59:50-07:00","id":1562637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562632#post1562632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking more that you might extend the discount on a permanent basis. I.e., everyone gets their three clan Disciplines at the reduced price, as well as one other inherited from their sire at the same price. Those four Disciplines would then always cost current rating x 5 instead of x7.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of instances where a bloodline commonly gets something out-of-clan (usually blood magic) where a fourth &quot;in-clan&quot; Discipline (at least in terms of price) would be beneficial. Then you can have Revised-era Ahrimanes with the core Disciplines of Animalism, Auspex and Protean, with Thaumaturgy as their &quot;sire&quot; Discipline, and it's a bit more manageable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not \u00d77 anymore, at least for now it's \u00d76.<br /> <br /> Let me do some calc. Assuming it was a choice between 4th dot and 4th discount:<br /> <br /> 1st dot is free vs 5 XP. 4th dot is better.<br /> 2nd dot is 12 XP vs 5 + 10 = 15 XP.<br /> 3rd dot is 12 + 18 = 30 XP vs 5 + 10 + 15 = 30 XP.<br /> <br /> Yeah, 4th dot is better for a dabbler, but above the 3rd dot discount is superior even with a smaller difference.<br /> <br /> Combining both would be interesting, but my worry is: how much would that impact buying OoC Disciplines? A vampire with 3 in-clans has still reason to explore OoC, but how much will this change if it's 4 in-clans with one of them being free choice?<br /> <br /> And how will that difference affect the game cycle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T01:54:57-07:00","id":1562721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562637#post1562637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not \u00d77 anymore, at least for now it's \u00d76.<br /> <br /> Let me do some calc. Assuming it was a choice between 4th dot and 4th discount:<br /> <br /> 1st dot is free vs 5 XP. 4th dot is better.<br /> 2nd dot is 12 XP vs 5 + 10 = 15 XP.<br /> 3rd dot is 12 + 18 = 30 XP vs 5 + 10 + 15 = 30 XP.<br /> <br /> Yeah, 4th dot is better for a dabbler, but above the 3rd dot discount is superior even with a smaller difference.<br /> <br /> Combining both would be interesting, but my worry is: how much would that impact buying OoC Disciplines? A vampire with 3 in-clans has still reason to explore OoC, but how much will this change if it's 4 in-clans with one of them being free choice?<br /> <br /> And how will that difference affect the game cycle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't know, honestly. It fits the &quot;more customisation&quot; thing, certainly, but it's going to be different. Presumably you'd still need ST permission for whichever Discipline you pick as fourth, but technically, you could pick any additional Disciplines you wanted with freebies in V1\u2013V20, and that wasn't totally borked. I'd have to play it to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T01:18:24-07:00","id":1562765,"title":"","content":"I certainly agree that vampires should be able to naturally see in the dark. That should have been a rule from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think that not changing VtM in that way is a \u201cfuck you\u201d to the fans. Making new editions is tricky, because you have to keep many things the same to please old fans and yet you have to change things enough to justify people investing in the new edition. <br /> <br /> Giving vampires natural night vision would seem to be a welcome and very simple change to make. Though once you make that change, Auspex 1 and Protean 1 become much less effective, in fact Protean 1 just about becomes worthless depending on the details of how Protean vs innate dark vision work. So maybe Protean 1 can be changed, though then we get a larger change in the system that maybe developers wanted to avoid. <br /> <br /> So, while I want vampires to see in the dark without a Discipline, I wouldn\u2019t judge developers for not doing it, especially since it\u2019s a rule that goes back to first edition.<br /> <br /> Personally, I do allow vampires to naturally see in the dark. It\u2019s a rule change I\u2019ve used for literal decades and I could easily continue using it if I end up playing 6th edition. Incidentally, I also have house rules for Protean too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T06:27:05-07:00","id":1562769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562476-6e-senses?p=1562765#post1562765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly agree that vampires should be able to naturally see in the dark. That should have been a rule from the beginning.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think that not changing VtM in that way is a \u201cfuck you\u201d to the fans. Making new editions is tricky, because you have to keep many things the same to please old fans and yet you have to change things enough to justify people investing in the new edition.<br /> <br /> Giving vampires natural night vision would seem to be a welcome and very simple change to make. Though once you make that change, Auspex 1 and Protean 1 become much less effective, in fact Protean 1 just about becomes worthless depending on the details of how Protean vs innate dark vision work. So maybe Protean 1 can be changed, though then we get a larger change in the system that maybe developers wanted to avoid.<br /> <br /> So, while I want vampires to see in the dark without a Discipline, I wouldn\u2019t judge developers for not doing it, especially since it\u2019s a rule that goes back to first edition.<br /> <br /> Personally, I do allow vampires to naturally see in the dark. It\u2019s a rule change I\u2019ve used for literal decades and I could easily continue using it if I end up playing 6th edition. Incidentally, I also have house rules for Protean too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take that but I doubt it was a reasoning that stopped the developers from making V6 vampires to see in the dark. They make much more drastic to the setting and Disciplines to be saying &quot;Oh no, deleting Eyes of the Beast is a step too far.&quot; I might be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}